* Syllabus

- [Syllabus](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LYd7QqGOU2_JR5QOWaAxWCwBB2cy16n57dSaVV6A3tc)
  - Big Data, Data Models
  - ETL and basic dev tools
    - Git / GitHub, Docker / Docker Compose
    - Data pipelines and ETL flavors
  - Relational DBs
  - NoSQL
    - E.g., HBase MongoDB
  - Data wrangling
    - E.g., Pandas, Parquet, Airflow
  - Computing frameworks
    - MapReduce, Spark, Dask
  - Parallel DBs
  - Cloud computing and AWS ecosystem
  - Graph DBs
    - E.g., Neo4j, Graph data processing
  - Streaming analytics
    - E.g., Apache Storm, Spark Streaming

* Tools We Will Learn To Use
- @Programming languages@
  - Python

- @Development tools@
  - Bash/Linux OS
  - Git: data model, branching
  - GitHub: Pull Requests (PR), issues
  - Jupyter notebooks
  - Docker

- @Big data tools@
  - Extract-Transform-Load (ETL) pipelines
  - Relational DBs (PostgreSQL)
  - NoSQL DBs (HBase, MongoDB, Couchbase, Redis)
  - Graph DBs (Neo4j, GraphX, Giraph)
  - Computing framework (Hadoop, Spark, Dask)
  - Workflow manager (Airflow)
  - Cloud services (AWS)

- @Tutorials@ for tools used in the class projects

